# Code owners for DnDOverlay.
#
# This has no effect until a second person is involved, and that is GitHub's behaviour
# rather than an oversight: GitHub never requests a review from the author of a pull
# request and does not let them approve their own. While the owner develops alone this
# file produces no review request at all - and the branch protection option "Require
# review from Code Owners" would not be ineffective but would make every own pull request
# unmergeable.
#
# Therefore: until the first outside contribution this file is a statement of intent, the
# option stays off, and the owner may bypass the pull request requirement. The force-push
# and deletion locks apply from day one. When a second contributor joins, both switches
# are tightened (Part 2).
#
# Syntax note: no "!" for exceptions, no "[ ]" ranges, no "#" escaped with "\" - three
# gitignore patterns that do NOT apply here. Several owners go on the same line.

